# Static IP assignments for devices
# Format: mac_address|ip_address|name
# These are applied as dnsmasq static leases on the router.
# IPs should be outside your DHCP pool or within it (dnsmasq reserves them).
#
# This is optional but useful for:
# - Consistent device identification in logs
# - Port forwarding
# - The parental control works on MAC addresses, so static IPs are not required

CHANGEME:MAC1|192.168.1.10|device_name
CHANGEME:MAC2|192.168.1.11|device_name
CHANGEME:MAC3|192.168.1.12|device_name

CHANGEME:MAC4|192.168.1.13|device_name
CHANGEME:MAC5|192.168.1.14|device_name
CHANGEME:MAC6|192.168.1.15|device_name
CHANGEME:MAC7|192.168.1.16|device_name
CHANGEME:MAC8|192.168.1.17|device_name
CHANGEME:MAC9|192.168.1.18|device_name